 Key Features & Projects Covered1. Ending Balance CalculatorConcept: Loop Control Structures (while loop).   Description: Calculates compound interest or running account balance over a designated number of months.   Functionality:Takes the initial starting balance and total number of months as user inputs.   Runs a pretest while loop to compute monthly interest accumulation based on a fixed rate.   Displays each month's running balance step-by-step inside a ListBox and outputs the final calculated balance in a label control.   2. Random Number GeneratorConcept: The Random Class.   Description: Generates unpredictable integer values within a specified range upon request.   Functionality:Instantiates a .NET Random object in memory.   Invokes the Next() method (e.g., rand.Next(100)) to pick a random integer.   Presents the generated value to the user inside a pop-up MessageBox.   3. Read Text File OutputConcept: Stream Reading (StreamReader) and Loop Detection.   Description: Opens a local text file and populates its line-by-line contents into a UI component.   Functionality:Establishes a stream connection to a target text file using File.OpenText().   Uses a while (!reader.EndOfStream) loop to iterate through every line until reaching the end of the file.   Reads each line via ReadLine() and populates it directly into a ListBox.   Safely closes the file stream inside a try-catch block to handle exceptions.   4. Save File ApplicationConcept: Stream Writing (StreamWriter) and SaveFileDialog Control.   Description: Lets users choose a file path interactively to create and save text data.   Functionality:Triggers the system's native Windows "Save As" modal using saveFileDialog.ShowDialog().   Checks if the user clicked OK (DialogResult.OK) or Cancel.   Creates the file at the chosen path using File.CreateText() and writes data lines via StreamWriter.WriteLine().   Flushes and closes the stream after writing to ensure file integrity.   
